<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Armistice of Villa Giusti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">Armistice</a> of Villa Giusti was signed on 3 November 1918 at a villa near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> on behalf of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a>, and took effect the next day. Coming after the Italian victory at Vittorio <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veneto">Veneto</a>, it ended the war on the Italian front while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> monarchy was already breaking apart.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/armistice-of-villa-giusti.jpg" alt="Armistice of Villa Giusti" width="320" height="302" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Evening Herald. Nov 4 1918 Tribune. Nov 4 1918 Webster City Freeman. Nov 4 1918 The Wheeling Intelligencer. Nov 4... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nov_1918_US_media_coverage_of_the_Empire_of_Austro-Hungary_exiting_the_WWI.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
